 8 blocks from rows 4 to 10. I want to index the values across various rows and columns. There seem to be rectangles from c6 to c15 that fit the criteria. I'm also considering patterns across separate regions for purely monochrome rectangles, aiming for a minimum of 5x5 dimensions.**Finding maximal rectangles**\n\nI’m working on qualifying regions and have identified some rectangles: from rows 2 to 7 and columns 4 to 9 is a 6x6 region, while rows 12 to 16 and columns 22 to 26 forms a 5x5. There are also potential 6x7 rectangles from rows 2 to 7 and columns 20 to 26, as well as from rows 17 to 22 and columns 10 to 16. I want to find maximal rectangles of the same color with dimensions of at least 5x5, using enumeration.","t":1793598802.5978427,"summary":true},{"type":"tool","name":"ipython","input":"# enumerate maximal-by-inclusion monochrome rectangles with >=5 height/width\nR=C=30\nrects=[]\nfor r1 in range(R):\n for r2 in range(r1+4,R):\n  for c1 in range(C):\n   for c2 in range(c1+4,C):\n    v=grid[r1][c1]\n    if all(grid[r][c]==v for r in range(r1,r2+1) for c in range(c1,c2+1)):\n     rects.append((r1,r2,c1,c2,v))\nlen(rects), rects[:30]","t":1793598802.5978427,"output":"(144, [(4, 8, 6, 10, 8), (4, 8, 6, 11, 8), (4, 8, 6, 12, 8), (4, 8, 6, 13, 8), (4, 8, 6, 14, 8), (4, 8, 6, 15, 8), (4, 8, 7, 11, 8), (4, 8, 7, 12, 8), (4, 8, 7, 13, 8), (4, 8, 7, 14, 8), (4, 8, 7, 15, 8), (4, 8, 8, 12, 8), (4, 8, 8, 13, 8), (4, 8, 8, 14, 8), (4, 8, 8, 15, 8), (4, 8, 9, 13, 8), (4, 8, 9, 14, 8), (4, 8, 9, 15, 8), (4, 8, 10, 14, 8), (4, 8, 10, 15, 8), (4, 8, 11, 15, 8), (4, 9, 6, 10, 8), (4, 9, 6, 11, 8), (4, 9, 6, 12, 8), (4, 9, 6, 13, 8), (4, 9, 6, 14, 8), (4, 9, 6, 15, 8), (4, 9, 7, 11, 8), (4, 9, 7, 12, 8), (4, 9, 7, 13, 8)])"},{"type":"reasoning","text":"**Identifying maximum rectangle**\n\nI'm focusing on how to identify the maximal rectangle by looking at bounding sizes without extending any side. I think I need to enumerate potential maximum area candidates to find the best one. It might involve checking different configurations to see which gives the largest area. My goal is to ensure I'm considering all possibilities to find the optimal solution effectively. I’ll begin by mapping out the candidates to move forward!","t":1793598806.1546905,"summary":true},{"type":"tool","name":"ipython","input":"# print candidate uniform rectangle largest area for each color, anchored patterns\nfor v in sorted(set(sum(grid,[]))):\n best=[]; area=0\n for r1 in range(R):\n  for r2 in range(r1,R):\n   for c1 in range(C):\n    for c2 in range(c1,C):\n     if all(grid[r][c]==v for r in range(r1,r2+1) for c in range(c1,c2+1)):\n      a=(r2-r1+1)*(c2-c1+1)\n      if a>area: area=a;best=[(r1,r2,c1,c2)]\n      elif a==area:best.append((r1,r2,c1,c2))\n print(v,area,best[:6])","t":1793598806.1546905,"output":"1 20 [(2, 5, 21, 25)]\n2 4 [(12, 12, 10, 13), (25, 25, 5, 8), (25, 26, 21, 22)]\n3 42 [(19, 25, 15, 20)]\n6 3 [(10, 12, 22, 22)]\n8 70 [(4, 10, 6, 15)]\n"},{"type":"tool","name":"ipython","input":"# identify maximal same-color rectangles >= 3x3 by brute force; list maximal boundaries\n","t":1793598813.0020595,"output":""}],"action":{"type":"demo"}},{"step":19,"kind":"observation","phase":"act","t0":1793598818.494,"t1":1793598844.524,"alias":"task-5833cda8","message":"Feedback since your last action:\nDemos received (request 2):\n\nDemo pair 2 input (30x30):\n6 8 6 8 8 8 8 6 6 3 8 6 2 3 8 1 2 8 1 3 8 3 3 6 6 1 2 6 2 2\n2 3 3 2 2 3 6 2 6 2 8 1 3 8 1 8 1 8 8 8 8 2 2 3 2 1 2 8 6 3\n2 3 8 2 3 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 3 8 2 6 6 2 8 3 8 8 3 2 3 3 3 2\n8 6 8 2 3 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 3 1 1 2 1 2 6 8 2 6 2 1 8 3 3 8\n6 8 6 2 3 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 3 3 3 8 1 1 2 1 8 3 8 2 3 6 8 2\n3 8 3 3 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 2 8 6 3 2 6 1 6 6 2 8 8 3 2 6 6\n2 6 3 2 8 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 8 3 8 3 3 6 3 1 8 8 1 2 3 1 8 8\n3 8 1 6 1 8 1 3 8 3 2 3 2 8 1 3 1 2 2 8 1 6 3 3 3 6 2 2 8 6\n8 3 3 8 3 8 2 2 8 8 8 8 8 1 1 6 3 3 6 2 2 6 1 3 3 6 3 1 3 3\n2 3 3 2 3 2 6 2 3 6 8 3 3 8 3 6 1 3 3 8 8 1 6 6 8 8 1 6 2 